## The 0.5ct Setting Multiplier — Why Setting Matters More Than Stone at This Size

**The 0.5ct Setting Multiplier is the budget principle that says: at 0.5ct, the setting costs more than the stone and dominates the final ring look.** A $900 stone in a $2,500 pavé halo setting reads like a $4,000+ ring. A $900 stone in a $500 bare prong setting reads like a $1,400 ring.

The math is simple. At 0.5ct, the stone face-up is 32 mm². A pavé halo adds 20+ small diamonds in a ring around it, expanding visible sparkle area to 60–80 mm². The halo nearly doubles perceived size without touching center-stone cost.

