## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a 0.5 carat marquise diamond cost?

0.5 carat marquise diamond cost starts at **$822** for natural I-VVS2 Very Good Cut GIA. Lab-grown starts at **$495** for IGI E-VVS1. Market ceiling is $1,958 for natural D-IF Ideal. Most honest-value picks sit in the $820–$950 band.

### What is the cheapest 0.5 carat marquise diamond?

The cheapest certified 0.5 carat marquise diamond in current market inventory is the **[$495 IGI E-VVS1 Very Good Cut lab-grown](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29703930?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**. The cheapest natural is **[$822 GIA I-VVS2 Very Good](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29422863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**.

### Is a 0.5 carat marquise too small for an engagement ring?

No. A 0.5 carat marquise measures 8.0 × 4.0 mm, which is 21% larger face-up than a 0.5 carat round diamond. Reads as a 0.75 carat round on the finger thanks to the Elongation Illusion. See our [marquise diamond size chart](/marquise-cut-diamond-size-chart) for every size comparison.

### What clarity should I buy at 0.5ct marquise?

**VVS2 is the clarity ceiling at 0.5ct.** Everything above VVS2 is invisible without a microscope. Buy G-VVS2 at $873 or H-VVS2 at $924 — anything above these grades is paying for certificate lines, not visible stone quality.

### What color grade is best for 0.5 carat marquise?

**G or H color** is the sweet spot. G color stays white in any metal setting; H color is clean in yellow or rose gold. Below I color, you may notice a slight tint in white gold. Above G, you are paying for colorlessness the eye can't distinguish at 0.5ct. Full logic in our [marquise diamond color guide](/marquise-diamond-color-guide).

### Is 0.5ct marquise worth it vs 0.75ct?

Depends on budget. 0.5ct marquise starts at $822; 0.75ct natural starts around $2,900. That is $2,000+ for 40% more face-up area. If the budget is under $1,500, 0.5ct is the honest entry point. If it stretches to $3,000+, 0.75ct is the stronger value tier.

### Does a 0.5 carat marquise bow-tie?

Yes, every marquise has some bow-tie — the dark zone across the middle. At 0.5ct the bow-tie is smaller and less noticeable than at 2ct+ because the whole stone is smaller. Always check the HD video on the retailer listing before buying. See [marquise diamond bow-tie](/marquise-diamond-bow-tie) for severity grading.

### Lab or natural at 0.5 carat marquise?

**Lab wins on value at 0.5ct.** The $495 IGI lab stone outspecs the $822 natural floor on both color (E vs I) and clarity (VVS1 vs VVS2). Natural wins only if origin matters to you or if you plan to resell — but resale at 0.5ct is weak for either.

### What is the Ideal cut on 0.5ct marquise?

"Ideal" on a 0.5ct marquise is a retailer label, not a GIA cut grade. GIA does not issue cut grades for fancy shapes like marquise. The label adds $38–$95 to the price. Verify polish and symmetry both read "Very Good" or "Excellent" on the GIA certificate before paying the premium.

### How big does a 0.5 carat marquise look on the finger?

A 0.5 carat marquise is 8.0 × 4.0 mm — about the size of a long rice grain. On a size 5 finger it covers 48% of the width lengthwise. Reads as a 0.75 carat round in apparent size because of the Elongation Illusion.

### What setting is best for 0.5 carat marquise?

**Pavé halo setting.** The halo adds 20+ small diamonds around the center stone. That expands visible sparkle area to 60–80 mm² — roughly double the bare stone's 32 mm². At 0.5ct, the halo nearly doubles perceived ring size for $800–$2,000. Full options in our [marquise halo engagement ring](/marquise-halo-engagement-ring) guide.

### Can I resell a 0.5 carat marquise diamond?

Resale is weak at this size. 0.5ct fancy-shape stones typically return 20–30% of the retail price in secondary market. Lab-grown resale is near-zero at 0.5ct. Buy for the ring, not the exit — budget-first buyers should accept the resale limit.

### What is the price per carat for 0.5 marquise?

At 0.5ct natural, price per carat runs **$1,644 to $3,916** across the full market band ($822–$1,958 divided by 0.5). That is 2–4x the per-carat rate of 1ct marquise ($4,049 ÷ 1 = $4,049/ct) because small-stone cutting still carries fixed labor cost.

